WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.350
- You and your brother
Shawn wrote "Scary Movie".

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:04.520
So did you like scary movies as kids?

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:05.380
'Cause I did not.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.090
- I hated scary movies and I
think that's why we wrote them

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:12.070
because first of all, I couldn't
understand why the killer,

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:14.280
these girls are running and
bolting through the woods

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.180
and this killer is just (whistles)

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.260
walking and taking his
time and going for a stroll

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:21.950
and they're all (breathes heavily).

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:23.010
And he still catches him.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.749
I don't get it.

00:00:24.749 --> 00:00:26.040
So I wasn't scared.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.120
The only one that really scared me

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.955
was "Nightmare on Elm Street"-

00:00:29.955 --> 00:00:31.112
- Me too!

00:00:31.112 --> 00:00:33.112
- Because I couldn't figure
out, like me and my brother

00:00:33.112 --> 00:00:34.680
Shawn, we started drinking
coffee, we didn't go to sleep.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.170
We was like nine and we
had my nephew at the time

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:41.390
when we watched it, we had it
on VCR and we got my little

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:44.367
nephew Craig, he was like four years old,

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:45.660
but he was thick and me and Shawn used him

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:48.589
as a teddy bear to watch the
movie 'cause we were scared.

00:00:48.589 --> 00:00:49.930
- (laughs) He was thick.

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:52.130
Wait, that one wrecked me.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:54.220
I would not even sit on a water bed

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.800
because of that Johnny Depp scene.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.123
Those were messed up movies, anyway.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.940
- I told you I started drinking
coffee at nine years old

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.300
thanks to that movie.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.430
- So Halloween is big in New York,

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:06.030
but you guys didn't celebrate
his kids though, right?

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:07.330
- No, my dad was Jehovah's Witness,

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:10.168
so we didn't really celebrate any holiday.

00:01:10.168 --> 00:01:12.220
So we didn't do that.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:15.840
And plus we really couldn't
afford the costumes.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.500
So me and my brother,
don't tell him my dad this,

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.909
well you can tell him now, he's 84,

00:01:20.909 --> 00:01:24.140
he can't whoop our behind
now, but when me and Shawn

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:27.047
switched clothes and I
would go and they'd be like,

00:01:27.047 --> 00:01:28.632
"Who are you?"

00:01:28.632 --> 00:01:29.800
And I'd be like, "I'm Shawn."

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:31.537
And he be like, "I'm Marlon."

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:33.730
Because we switched clothes.

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:35.320
So it wasn't really a costume.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:36.780
It wasn't, we was trick or treating,

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.593
we was just begging basically.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.360
- We had no money, so I was queen

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.280
of just putting a sheet
on and cutting holes.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.840
I'm a ghost, give me candy.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.610
- Girl, you know what
kind of behind whoopin'

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:52.006
I would have got for cutting
holes in the sheet, you crazy.

00:01:52.006 --> 00:01:53.190
(laughter)

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:57.330
My mother like, "That's my
good sheet, you know better!"

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:59.290
- Oh my god. (laughs)

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:00.760
I don't know, it was like the easiest,

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:02.490
cheapest thing I could do.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.360
So my mom probably never
knew that, whatever,

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.310
they were my sheets, she never saw 'em.

